6. Simplest form (rules 1, 2, 8, 10): the fix is the smallest that works, adds no helper or layer, and keeps every line at 120
   characters or fewer.
7. Readability bar (owner Rule 16): a junior to mid-level developer must read the NEW line and understand it quickly. A line
   you cannot explain in one plain sentence is a finding.
8. Comments (owner Rule 17): a comment added that restates the code, or more comment than a competent human would write, is a
   finding. Comments say why, briefly.
End with one line: Verdict: GREEN or RED, then your numbered findings.

